{"id": "EUVD-2026-82083", "enisaUuid": "a757009c-0cbf-344f-bba6-66749d7b9b5c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nclk: mediatek: pllfh: Fix IO remapping leak in register_pllfhs error path\n\nWhen mtk_clk_register_pllfhs function fails to register a PLL, it\nunregisters all PLLs and cleans up itself in its error path before\nreturning, so the function callers don't need to do it.\n\nBut contrary to mtk_clk_unregister_pllfhs function, that does almost\nthe same sequence, it does not free the IO memory mapped on fhctl node,\nleading to a leak.\n\nFix this leak by factorizing the cleanup sequence in a new private\nfunction and use it both mtk_clk_register_pllfhs and\nmtk_clk_unregister_pllfhs functions.\n\nAlso, change the loop index start value to avoid the -1 operation on\nindex at each loop.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e3e93bc718c4fea556d7ca5fba07ab3511c9918", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/111235106099019b8a8d1947dc5c2674e0329ffa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d35e45e5bad4fabcf122126402b6c6dcb4379672", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fea0b4fd891a2af77b55e05b950e7ea55b5d234e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/540d91480bcb1b28a62d7023aa70947ea44c55b9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hw67-72fp-vf5f", "CVE-2026-90422"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17bdade8-43d1-3efe-bf4d-5ef8358a5a68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "25de1329-579b-3477-8913-4c44e5cdffb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7964de8a8ea800910fdd4e365c42a9e7d5c54aa <d35e45e5bad4fabcf122126402b6c6dcb4379672"}, {"id": "35500663-a705-3505-ad8b-cceba1764c7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "3752ac08-a256-305f-a5a5-8fb6d4161a26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7964de8a8ea800910fdd4e365c42a9e7d5c54aa <111235106099019b8a8d1947dc5c2674e0329ffa"}, {"id": "4e59edc1-5c57-3115-a26b-88fc942de4fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.2"}, {"id": "8732a43a-87a4-304f-a768-e1cd6c1ad943", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "a07135ae-317a-3ebc-abb5-b1afc9157fb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7964de8a8ea800910fdd4e365c42a9e7d5c54aa <6e3e93bc718c4fea556d7ca5fba07ab3511c9918"}, {"id": "af646540-6957-332f-a19d-aa54d7ec87bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b42e0b78-d4d8-30a3-827c-20a013c7f485", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "bb330356-f71d-3398-9934-00058569e779", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "bfd58082-d47f-3712-9828-129d10b849e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7964de8a8ea800910fdd4e365c42a9e7d5c54aa <540d91480bcb1b28a62d7023aa70947ea44c55b9"}, {"id": "e96f8501-a56c-39b3-8481-0bc6605b9242", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d7964de8a8ea800910fdd4e365c42a9e7d5c54aa <fea0b4fd891a2af77b55e05b950e7ea55b5d234e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a649c7fc-5c8f-3b7d-9bcb-e79b213c9623", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}